## Objective

To understand the interface of Adobe Photoshop and learn to use basic tools for creating designs with shapes, colours, and text.

## Tools Used

* Move Tool
* Marquee Tool
* Lasso Tool
* Brush Tool
* Eraser Tool
* Shape Tool
* Text Tool

## Steps

1. Open Adobe Photoshop.
2. Create a new document with a size of 1200 × 800 pixels.
3. Use the Shape Tool to draw different shapes.
4. Apply different colours to the shapes.
5. Use the Text Tool to add a heading and student details.
6. Arrange the shapes and text properly.
7. Save the editable file in PSD format.
8. Export the final design as a JPG image.
